{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1174790833#1_2588206772","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage is about salsa as a food condiment becoming the best-selling condiment in America and outselling ketchup, but it does not explain why salsa was not noticed in America.","learned":"For the food interpretation, salsa became highly popular in the U.S.; it began outselling ketchup in 1992, yet some people still failed to appreciate its popularity."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1174790833#1_2588206772","reason":"The snippet is about Americans failing to appreciate salsa's popularity; the full document may contain a direct explanation for why salsa's prominence went unnoticed."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1174790833#1_2588206772"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1174790833#1_2588206772","document":"WHAT’S THE MOST POPULAR CONDIMENT IN AMERICA? - The Loco Life ... WHAT’S THE MOST POPULAR CONDIMENT IN AMERICA? Loco Living WHAT’S THE MOST POPULAR CONDIMENT IN AMERICA? Also in Loco Living 5 Things You Must Do In Albuqurque Healthiest Salsa To Buy Salsa Claus is Delivering Hot Boxes  ... India is known for chutneys, and soy sauce is the condiment of choice in many Asian cuisines. But which condiment is the most popular in the United States? If you guessed ketchup, you’re dead wrong. Barbecue sauce has been beaten, too, and even ranch dressing doesn’t come out on top. The best-selling condiment in America in terms of annual sales is salsa. Every year, Americans buy more than $460 million worth of salsa, consuming it on everything from chips to tacos to eggs. Salsa first began to outsell ketchup back in 1992 but many people still fail to appreciate just how popular the spicy sauce has become. Salsa, of course, did not originate in the United States. Salsa is the Spanish word for “sauce” and is traditionally used to describe all types of sauce-like condiments used in cuisine. Today, we typically only call red and green sauces with tomato or tomatillo bases “salsa.”","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
