{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_987335278#6_1782626290","relevance":2,"reason":"The PBS Latin Music USA passage is related and provides indirect support for a language/mainstream barrier: Marc Anthony's English-language album cemented his mainstream appeal, while his salsa work was in Spanish. However, it does not directly explain why salsa as a genre was not noticed in America.","learned":"A higher-quality source suggests English-language crossover helped Latin/salsa artists reach the U.S. mainstream, implying Spanish-language salsa had more limited mainstream notice."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"latin music usa\" salsa \"mainstream\" \"english-language\")","reason":"Search within/around the PBS Latin Music USA source family for more direct evidence about salsa, English-language crossover, and mainstream American notice."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"latin music usa\" salsa \"mainstream\" \"english-language\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_987335278#4_1782623624","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2514","rank":2,"snippet":"The two young artists helped bring Latinos and non-Latinos back to dance floors across America as <cover>Salsa swept the country once again. Sergio George then produced India’s 1994 album, Dicen que Soy (They Say I Am), with feminist themes in many of the tracks. It was “India doing her thing,” George said. She became a legend to Latinos, but has never crossed to the mainstream market. Some critics put it down to her “controversial” persona. Sony producer Tommy Mottola has praised India’s voice, calling it “one of the most fascinating voices I have ever heard,” but he felt that “ [her] rhythms are more narrow than the pop rhythms of Latin music, and that they didn’t work in English.” Still, her career as a musician flourished. In 1996, she worked with Tito Puente on Jazzin, an English-language album of swing classics with a Latin twist on RMM Records. She also released India:\" , \"start_char\": 2644.000000 , \"title\": \"La India and Marc Anthony | The Legends | Latin Music USA</cover>\" , \"url\": \"http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/latinmusicusa/legends/la-india-and-","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_987335278#6_1782626290","rank":1,"relevance":2}]}}
